# Django admin custom pages & model registration

## Custom admin pages

Staff tool views (non-ModelAdmin) must be annotated so they get a URL **and** appear in the Tools block on `/admin/`.

### Do

```python
from news.admin_custom_pages import custom_admin_page

@custom_admin_page(
    name="news_my_tool",
    path="news/my-tool/",
    title="My tool",
    description="One-line what this page does.",
)
@require_http_methods(["GET", "POST"])
def my_tool_view(request: HttpRequest) -> HttpResponse:
    ...
```

- Put the view in `web/news/admin_*.py` and ensure the module is imported before `patch_admin_site()` (e.g. import from `admin_ops.py` like theme analysis)
- Prefer linking from the admin index (automatic); changelist shortcuts are optional extras
- Keep `web/news/test_admin_index.py` green — it asserts every registered custom page is on the index

### Don't

- Mount custom admin URLs only via ad-hoc `get_urls` paths without `@custom_admin_page`
- Hard-code a parallel list of tools on the index template
- Rely on a cursor rule alone without the registry + test

## ModelAdmin registration

Every concrete model in `news.models` must have a `ModelAdmin` in `web/news/admin.py` (`@admin.register`). `test_all_concrete_news_models_registered` enforces this.
